Our approach begins with a Hybrid delivery model, combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure suited to public and health procurement. This methodology has been successfully applied in past references, such as regional council and mutual health insurer projects. We propose the following key milestones and deliverables: Framing Phase, Design Phase, Pilot Phase, Generalisation Phase, and Run Phase. Each phase will include specific deliverables, including a detailed project plan, functional specification document, user interface prototypes, data integration plan, training for hospital staff, and change management support.

Our proposed solution, Atelier, is designed to provide fast response times, with a median latency of 1.3 seconds and a p95 latency of less than 2 seconds for common single-document queries. We offer 24/7 operation on the appropriate hosting tier, with an active-active setup across two availability zones to ensure high availability. Our architecture includes standard connectors for SIH and DPI integration, as well as custom adapters where needed. We will deploy our solution on OuraneCloud, a SecNumCloud-qualified provider within the EU, ensuring that all data is hosted within the European Union with no transfer outside the EU.

To meet the tender's regulatory requirements, we have implemented various security controls and compliance measures. We rely on our existing certifications, including ISO 27001 and ISO 27701, which cover the development, delivery, and operations of our services. Our hosting partner, OuraneCloud, holds the French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification, ensuring that our infrastructure meets the necessary standards for hosting health data in France. We also provide encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, as well as key management on EU-based infrastructure, pseudonymisation capabilities, and configurable retention policies to protect sensitive health data.

Our solution is designed as an assistance tool, with no clinical or medico-administrative decision automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional. We ensure that our system does not require medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR) and flag any use case that could approach the medical-device threshold, addressing the implications for liability and positioning.

